# React web with Vite

## Setup

- Start from `npm create vite@latest -- --template react-ts`, then apply the team configs from `configs/` (tsconfig, ESLint, Prettier, Vite, Vitest).
- Use `@vitejs/plugin-react`. Turn on the React Compiler when the team agrees to (follow the React Compiler docs for the current Vite setup); then drop manual memoization.
- Path alias `@/` → `src/`, defined once in `tsconfig.app.json` `paths` and mirrored in `vite.config.ts` `resolve.alias`.
- Node version pinned in `.nvmrc` and `package.json` `engines`.

## Environment variables

- Only variables prefixed `VITE_` reach the client, and they are public.
- Declare their types in `src/vite-env.d.ts` (`interface ImportMetaEnv`) and parse them once in `src/lib/env.ts`.
- `.env.local` for personal overrides (ignored by git); `.env.example` committed.

## Routing

- Use the project's router (React Router or TanStack Router). Lazy-load every route component.
- Each route gets its own error boundary (`errorElement` / `errorComponent`) and a loading fallback.
- Read and write filters through typed search params.
- Set the document title per route.

## Styling

- Use the project's approach consistently: Tailwind CSS, CSS Modules or a component library (MUI, shadcn/ui, Mantine). Don't mix approaches in one feature.
- Design tokens (colours, spacing, radius, typography) live in one place: Tailwind theme or CSS custom properties. No hard-coded hex values in components.
- Mobile-first, responsive layouts. Test at 320 px, 768 px and 1280 px.
- Support dark mode through tokens if the product has it.
- Class names are composed with a helper (`clsx` / `cn`), not string concatenation.

## Build and deploy

- `npm run build` runs `tsc -b` before `vite build`, so a type error fails the build.
- Check bundle size on pull requests (`rollup-plugin-visualizer` or a size-limit check).
- Generate source maps for monitoring but don't serve them publicly (upload them, then delete or restrict them).
- Serve with long-lived cache headers for hashed assets and `no-cache` for `index.html`.
- Configure security headers on the host: CSP, `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Referrer-Policy`, `Permissions-Policy`, HSTS.

## Browser APIs

- Guard browser-only APIs when code may run in tests or SSR: check `typeof window !== 'undefined'`.
- Clean up listeners, observers and timers in effect cleanups.
- Use `AbortController` for fetches and listeners tied to a component.

## SEO and metadata (if the app is public)

- Unique `<title>` and meta description per route; React 19 lets you render `<title>` and `<meta>` in components.
- If SEO matters for content pages, consider a framework with server rendering instead of a pure Vite SPA.
